{"affected_paths": ["agent_cost/aggregate.py", "README.md"], "claim_kind": "decision_record", "conformance_status": "matched", "contradicting_refs": [], "epistemic_status": "recorded_decision", "observation_id": "OBS-006", "origin": "recorded", "provenance": [{"content_digest": "a2d26673aa9122f441c92c4d1fe7662bfa6dceda98a862ae7136114f45a8cb8c", "extraction_method": "static-read-source", "observed_at": "2026-08-15T00:00:00Z", "repo_commit": "4260cba446ee1a71d1fc0605e3e2bf8ca8a78ed5", "selector": "price_fact (module docstring)", "source_kind": "source", "uri": "agent_cost/aggregate.py"}, {"content_digest": "6b3236a0d35fcae635a102cf2e6dc6d5776002fe78354877d157f94a4e6f27f6", "extraction_method": "static-read-source", "observed_at": "2026-08-15T00:00:00Z", "repo_commit": "4260cba446ee1a71d1fc0605e3e2bf8ca8a78ed5", "selector": "## What this measures, and what it doesn't", "source_kind": "spec", "uri": "README.md"}], "review_status": "unreviewed", "revision_digest": "16eaf264b1d55bf1a65c674b91c0e674459a8ad6f689553f36fe60758368e89e", "statement": "Pricing an unknown-TTL cache write at the 5-minute rate as an explicit lower bound -- instead of guessing the more expensive 1-hour rate, or averaging the two -- is a deliberate design decision, recorded in both price_fact's own docstring and the README's \"What this measures\" section, so a reader of the output number knows it is a floor, not a best-effort midpoint.", "subject_refs": ["price_fact"], "supporting_refs": [], "topic_id": "T-02", "valid_at_commit": "4260cba446ee1a71d1fc0605e3e2bf8ca8a78ed5"}
{"affected_paths": ["agent_cost/readers/codex.py"], "claim_kind": "behavior", "conformance_status": "matched", "contradicting_refs": [], "epistemic_status": "single_source_observation", "observation_id": "OBS-007", "origin": "reconstructed", "provenance": [{"content_digest": "010ba51f52092ad01f1effd88f0ba084467b609dae4469ce41c797a1f080109b", "extraction_method": "static-read-source", "observed_at": "2026-08-15T00:00:00Z", "repo_commit": "4260cba446ee1a71d1fc0605e3e2bf8ca8a78ed5", "selector": "parse_rollout_facts", "source_kind": "source", "uri": "agent_cost/readers/codex.py"}], "review_status": "unreviewed", "revision_digest": "b3e7a3e5c998d2744b23ee626b2a995e14a5d6431a3691cc3b20a34c02bb7ae3", "statement": "The Codex CLI reader (parse_rollout_facts) never emits a cache_write_5m, cache_write_1h, or cache_write_unknown fact for any event -- it only ever constructs Fact objects with token_kind \"input_nocache\", \"cache_read\", or \"output\". This matches the README's claim that Codex exposes no cache-write signal at all, but is recorded here from a direct, single-pass static read of the reader module rather than from a test that asserts the negative (no test in tests/test_reader_codex.py checks that \"cache_write\" never appears in a fact's token_kind).", "subject_refs": ["parse_rollout_facts"], "supporting_refs": [], "topic_id": "T-02", "valid_at_commit": "4260cba446ee1a71d1fc0605e3e2bf8ca8a78ed5"}
{"affected_paths": ["agent_cost/aggregate.py"], "claim_kind": "behavior", "conformance_status": "matched", "contradicting_refs": [], "epistemic_status": "execution_verified", "observation_id": "OBS-008", "origin": "reconstructed", "provenance": [{"content_digest": "4fa19557fb67f561bd959564173e7f05ba63205d1871683f11d9ff521956b34a", "extraction_method": "static-read-test-assertions", "observed_at": "2026-08-15T00:00:00Z", "repo_commit": "4260cba446ee1a71d1fc0605e3e2bf8ca8a78ed5", "selector": "test_price_fact_unknown_model_is_unpriced", "source_kind": "test", "uri": "tests/test_aggregate.py"}, {"content_digest": "4fa19557fb67f561bd959564173e7f05ba63205d1871683f11d9ff521956b34a", "extraction_method": "static-read-test-assertions", "observed_at": "2026-08-15T00:00:00Z", "repo_commit": "4260cba446ee1a71d1fc0605e3e2bf8ca8a78ed5", "selector": "test_price_fact_codex_cache_write_is_unpriced", "source_kind": "test", "uri": "tests/test_aggregate.py"}, {"content_digest": "440f06b2791b2326117807aaf47ea8889dcf552efa482b8f2593a7bd79fc01fd", "extraction_method": "static-read-test-assertions", "observed_at": "2026-08-15T00:00:00Z", "repo_commit": "4260cba446ee1a71d1fc0605e3e2bf8ca8a78ed5", "selector": "test_gpt_5_5_cache_write_is_unpriced", "source_kind": "test", "uri": "tests/test_rates.py"}], "review_status": "unreviewed", "revision_digest": "3300b6be1ba7f7b96a0f9d5ef1fbc19407cf4ac5f8d9ea8bceceed40ff7aef5c", "statement": "price_fact() returns (None, \"unpriced\", None) -- never a guessed number -- both when the fact's model_key does not resolve against the catalog at all, and when the model resolves but the specific token-kind rate field for the covering rate period is None (e.g. OpenAI models carry no cache_write_5m rate at all, so a cache-write fact against gpt-5.5 is unpriced even though the model itself is known).", "subject_refs": ["price_fact"], "supporting_refs": [], "topic_id": "T-03", "valid_at_commit": "4260cba446ee1a71d1fc0605e3e2bf8ca8a78ed5"}
{"affected_paths": ["agent_cost/aggregate.py"], "claim_kind": "behavior", "conformance_status": "matched", "contradicting_refs": [], "epistemic_status": "execution_verified", "observation_id": "OBS-009", "origin": "reconstructed", "provenance": [{"content_digest": "4fa19557fb67f561bd959564173e7f05ba63205d1871683f11d9ff521956b34a", "extraction_method": "static-read-test-assertions", "observed_at": "2026-08-15T00:00:00Z", "repo_commit": "4260cba446ee1a71d1fc0605e3e2bf8ca8a78ed5", "selector": "test_build_rows_mixed_priced_and_unpriced_marks_row_unpriced", "source_kind": "test", "uri": "tests/test_aggregate.py"}], "review_status": "unreviewed", "revision_digest": "efc505a68ff4748f086c60d755fc00ed9bdbbbf88fb16b1f2d6333c7ba0c5639", "statement": "build_rows() marks an entire grouped row \"unpriced\" as soon as any one of the facts folded into that bucket is unpriced, even if other facts in the same bucket priced normally -- a row is never reported as fully priced when part of its token count actually wasn't.", "subject_refs": ["build_rows"], "supporting_refs": [], "topic_id": "T-03", "valid_at_commit": "4260cba446ee1a71d1fc0605e3e2bf8ca8a78ed5"}
{"affected_paths": ["agent_cost/aggregate.py"], "claim_kind": "invariant", "conformance_status": "matched", "contradicting_refs": [], "epistemic_status": "single_source_observation", "observation_id": "OBS-010", "origin": "reconstructed", "provenance": [{"content_digest": "a2d26673aa9122f441c92c4d1fe7662bfa6dceda98a862ae7136114f45a8cb8c", "extraction_method": "static-read-source", "observed_at": "2026-08-15T00:00:00Z", "repo_commit": "4260cba446ee1a71d1fc0605e3e2bf8ca8a78ed5", "selector": "_STATUS_RANK", "source_kind": "source", "uri": "agent_cost/aggregate.py"}], "review_status": "unreviewed", "revision_digest": "aeb44fa67c5413192e5aa7da87731fd650804b4901ebb149e22feaf2d5559f69", "statement": "build_rows()'s row.pricing_status ranking is defined in code as a full three-way order -- unpriced (rank 0) beats lower_bound (rank 1) beats priced (rank 2), via _STATUS_RANK -- so a row containing both a lower_bound fact and a plain priced fact should end up \"lower_bound\", not \"priced\". Only the unpriced-over-priced half of this ordering is exercised by an existing test (test_build_rows_mixed_priced_and_unpriced_marks_row_unpriced); no test in tests/test_aggregate.py builds a row from a mix of a lower_bound fact and a priced fact, so the lower_bound-vs-priced half of the ranking is confirmed only by reading _STATUS_RANK and build_rows() directly, not by execution.", "subject_refs": ["build_rows", "_STATUS_RANK"], "supporting_refs": [], "topic_id": "T-03", "valid_at_commit": "4260cba446ee1a71d1fc0605e3e2bf8ca8a78ed5"}
